    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.extra, mini.pick\n\n### Description\n\nInconsistent behavior for different scopes of `MiniExtra.pickers.lsp`.  While `refrences` works as expected, `workspace_symbol` and `document_symbol` cannot be matched/selected.\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.10.1\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Set up `mini.pick` and `mini.extra` as standalone plugins with [lazy.nvim](https://github.com/folke/lazy.nvim) as in the [document](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/readmes/mini-extra.md#installation).\r\n2. Configure any LSP server using [nvim-lspconfig](https://github.com/neovim/nvim-lspconfig)\r\n3. Try to pick LSP symbols and references, then try to move up/down or enter some characters.\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n`workspace_symbol` and `document_symbol` scopes can be fuzzy-matched/selected similar to `references`.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nPressing any key close the floating window.\r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0254fdc8-77cc-428e-bdeb-f2c90464a42f\r\n\r\n",
